{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"options":{"content":"","images":{},"widgets":{}},"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"We will solve this by integrating by parts. We know that \n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u(x)v\\,^\\prime(x)dx = u(x)v(x)-\\int u\\,^\\prime(x)v(x)dx\\,$.\n\nWe can rewrite this as\n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u\\ dv = uv-\\int v\\ du\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this problem we will let $~u = x~$ and $~dv=e^{-x} dx\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Then $~du = dx~$ and $~v = \\displaystyle\\int e^{-x}dx = -e^{-x}$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Integration by parts gives\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\int^5_0 xe^{-x}dx =x\\cdot\\big(-e^{-x}\\big)\\Bigg]_0^5-\\int^5_0\\big(-e^{-x}\\big)dx$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~~= \\Big(-xe^{-x}-e^{-x}\\Big)\\Bigg]^5_0 $\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~~= -e^{-x}(x+1)\\Bigg]^5_0$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~~=-6e^{-5}-(-1\\cdot1)=-6e^{-5}+1$","images":{},"widgets":{}}],"question":{"content":"Evaluate $~~\\displaystyle\\int^5_0 xe^{-x}dx\\,$.\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-6e^{-5}+1$","correct":true},{"content":"$-4e^{-5}+1$","correct":false},{"content":"$-5e^{-5}-1$","correct":false},{"content":"$-5e^{-5}+1$","correct":false}],"displayCount":null,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"type":"radio","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
